JetSpec++ first-pass (J0) context-token initialization for vLLM's DFlash speculator, plus draft-step dump
instrumentation. Used for "A Short-Context Drafter on Long-Context Reasoning: Testing JetSpec++ on Qwen3.8-27B",
https://artus.ai/2026/10/31/jetspec-long-context.html (31 October 2026).

Base: vLLM c50aca14416ef29f6ed0ed256302f30646726dcd, one file:
  vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/speculator.py
Patched file sha256: 0f0a4d209568e41ee28389b33bd30803babee67cea28730e3475680cc1343974 (the file the test ran).
Apply in a vLLM checkout at that commit with `git apply vllm-dflash-jetspec-j0.patch`. The test mounted the patched
file over the same path in a vLLM nightly image built from that commit.

Both switches are environment variables and default to off, which leaves vLLM's behavior unchanged.

VLLM_DFLASH_CTX_NOISE=1
  Fills the draft block's non-anchor query slots with tokens from the committed context instead of vLLM's mask
  token, following the first pass of JetSpec++'s released code (hao-ai-lab/JetSpec @673267e4,
  jetspec/methods/jetspec_plus_plus/context.py, build_random_context_block_token_ids, mode "kth"). Slot 0 stays the
  anchor. Slot k takes the committed token at index r mod L: r is a fixed pseudo-random number per request slot and
  k, and L is the number of committed tokens including the anchor. The draws use Triton's generator, so they are
  not bit-identical to the released code's CPU generator. A [max_num_seqs, max_model_len] int32 history holds the
  committed tokens. It is written from each step's accepted tokens and the anchor before the draw, so no rejected or
  future token is read.

VLLM_DFLASH_DUMP=DIR with VLLM_DFLASH_DUMP_STEPS=N
  For the first N single-request steps, saves the target positions and input ids, the drafter's input hidden states
  (the concatenated target-layer taps), the rejected and sampled counts, the drafter's query ids and positions and
  the draft tokens to DIR/stepNNNN.pt, for comparison with a reference implementation. It copies to the CPU and so
  synchronizes: use it for checks, not timing. It also dumps the context-only steps of non-final prefill chunks. With
  CUDA graphs on, vLLM's startup warm-up request drafts too and gets dumped; skip those steps when comparing.

The patch also logs the draft KV cache dtype of every drafter attention layer at load.

Drafter: JetSpec/jetspec-plus-plus-qwen3p8-27b @3147a351, weights unchanged. vLLM reads the causal draft head from
dflash_config.causal, while the released config.json spells it causal_head, so add "causal": true to dflash_config in
a local copy of config.json. That is the only config change.

Serving flags for the drafter (15 draft tokens; the test also ran 7):
  --speculative-config '{"method":"dflash","model":"<drafter dir>","num_speculative_tokens":15,"kv_cache_dtype":"auto"}'
With "kv_cache_dtype":"auto" the draft KV cache stays BF16 even when the target uses an FP8 KV cache.

Research code, run only for this test: one RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, max-num-seqs 4, single-stream benchmarks. Other
batch sizes and GPUs are untested. License: Apache-2.0, as vLLM.

